[{"name":"/Pages/Deck","nodes":[{"id":"dkPage","type":"Page","parameters":{"title":"The deck","urlPath":"deck"},"ports":[],"children":[{"id":"dkGround","type":"Group","parameters":{"width":{"value":100,"unit":"%"},"sizeMode":"contentHeight","minHeight":{"value":100,"unit":"vh"},"flexDirection":"column","alignItems":"center","backgroundColor":"var(--background)","paddingTop":"var(--space-4)","paddingBottom":"var(--space-16)"},"ports":[],"children":[{"id":"dkShell","type":"Group","parameters":{"width":{"value":100,"unit":"%"},"maxWidth":{"value":560,"unit":"px"},"sizeMode":"contentHeight","flexDirection":"column","rowGap":"var(--space-5)","paddingLeft":"var(--space-4)","paddingRight":"var(--space-4)"},"ports":[],"children":[{"id":"dkHomeBtn","type":"net.noodl.controls.button","parameters":{"label":"← Spreads","backgroundColor":"transparent","color":"var(--muted-foreground)","borderStyle":"none","paddingLeft":"0","paddingRight":"var(--space-2)","paddingTop":"var(--space-2)","paddingBottom":"var(--space-2)","fontSize":"var(--text-sm)","fontWeight":"var(--font-medium)","sizeMode":"contentSize"},"ports":[],"children":[]},{"id":"dkBrowse","type":"Group","parameters":{"width":{"value":100,"unit":"%"},"sizeMode":"contentHeight","flexDirection":"column","rowGap":"var(--space-4)"},"ports":[],"children":[{"id":"dkEyebrow","type":"Text","parameters":{"text":"The deck","fontSize":"var(--text-xs)","fontWeight":"var(--font-semibold)","letterSpacing":"var(--tracking-widest)","textTransform":"uppercase","color":"var(--primary)"},"ports":[],"children":[]},{"id":"dkTitle","type":"Text","parameters":{"text":"How the deck works","fontFamily":"var(--font-serif)","fontSize":"var(--text-3xl)","lineHeight":"var(--leading-tight)","color":"var(--foreground)"},"ports":[],"children":[]},{"id":"dkP1","type":"Text","parameters":{"text":"A tarot deck has 78 cards. 22 of them are the Major Arcana: named cards like The Fool, The Lovers and Death. They stand for the big themes in a life.","fontSize":"var(--text-base)","lineHeight":"var(--leading-relaxed)","color":"var(--foreground)"},"ports":[],"children":[]},{"id":"dkP2","type":"Text","parameters":{"text":"The other 56 are four suits of 14, like playing cards: Wands, Cups, Swords and Pentacles. Each suit covers one part of life, and the picker below says which.","fontSize":"var(--text-base)","lineHeight":"var(--leading-relaxed)","color":"var(--foreground)"},"ports":[],"children":[]},{"id":"dkP3","type":"Text","parameters":{"text":"The numbers mean roughly the same in every suit. An Ace is a start, a Five is a struggle, and a Ten is the end of something, or too much of it. The Page, Knight, Queen and King are people, or ways of handling things.","fontSize":"var(--text-base)","lineHeight":"var(--leading-relaxed)","color":"var(--foreground)"},"ports":[],"children":[]},{"id":"dkP4","type":"Text","parameters":{"text":"A card that comes out upside down usually means the blocked or inward side of it.","fontSize":"var(--text-base)","lineHeight":"var(--leading-relaxed)","color":"var(--foreground)"},"ports":[],"children":[]},{"id":"dkP5","type":"Text","parameters":{"text":"None of it predicts anything. A card gives the person a theme to talk about.","fontSize":"var(--text-base)","lineHeight":"var(--leading-relaxed)","color":"var(--muted-foreground)"},"ports":[],"children":[]},{"id":"dkLookTitle","type":"Text","parameters":{"text":"Look up a card","fontFamily":"var(--font-serif)","fontSize":"var(--text-2xl)","color":"var(--foreground)","marginTop":"var(--space-4)"},"ports":[],"children":[]},{"id":"dkPicker","type":"/Cards/Picker","parameters":{},"ports":[],"children":[]},{"id":"dkRandomBtn","type":"net.noodl.controls.button","parameters":{"label":"Draw a random card","backgroundColor":"transparent","color":"var(--foreground)","borderRadius":"var(--radius-full)","borderStyle":"solid","borderWidth":"var(--border-1)","borderColor":"var(--border-control)","paddingLeft":"var(--space-6)","paddingRight":"var(--space-6)","padding